    "body": "Height trace at upstream/main d08e9eda (source inspection, not a machine run):\n\nPencil reads the raw facet normals in finishing3d/pencil.rs::loci. Reversing every facet negates both opposite-vertex plane tests, exchanging concave and convex candidates. The center offset is 2*r*(na+nb)/|na+nb|^2, so reversing both normals negates the offset. The emitted tip height is edge.z + offset.z - r. crease.rs::rests then checks the bottom window, clearance, unsigned distance to all nearby triangles, and both contact feet; these checks do not establish which side of a closed body is material. On an inward top cube edge at z=10 with r=1, the candidate center is at z=9 and its tip at z=8, inside the body. Resting checks may trim or reject a run, but cannot be treated as an orientation check.\n\nDeburr reads the mirrored raw-normal test in finishing3d/deburr.rs::deburr. Reversal exchanges the selected crease set. Its tip height remains edge.z - width/tan(included_angle/2), clipped to the programmed window. For width=0.5 and a 90-degree cone, an edge at z=10 yields tip z=9.5. Steep edges are skipped. The height formula does not reverse with winding, but a concave edge can be selected instead of an exposed convex edge.\n\nThe import fix turns each closed, consistently wound negative-volume body outward before either generator receives it. Open, mixed, non-manifold and zero-volume bodies retain the existing behavior. No claim about a full posted-program safety proof follows from this source trace.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
